{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH2Wedderburn","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH2Wedderburn","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH2AlgebraInstance","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.isSemisimpleRing_of_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.isSemisimpleRing_of_roots","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2Wedderburn.lean#L91-L98","doc":"**Semisimplicity of H₂(q) over a field, given generic roots\n(sorry-free).**  Transfer `IsSemisimpleRing (K × K)` along the\nWedderburn isomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.wedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.wedderburn","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2Wedderburn.lean#L51-L89","doc":"**The rank-2 Wedderburn decomposition (sorry-free).**  Given the two\nroots `lp`, `lm` of the Hecke quadratic with invertible difference\n(`d` its inverse), the paired characters give an `R`-algebra\nisomorphism `H₂(q) ≃ R × R`.  The two factors are the Wedderburn\nblocks of the partitions `(2)` and `(1,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.character_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.character_apply","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2Wedderburn.lean#L48-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.character","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2Wedderburn.lean#L36-L46","doc":"The **character** of `H2A R h` at a root `l` of the Hecke quadratic\n`x² = h·x + 1`: the ring homomorphism `a + b·σ ↦ a + l·b`\n(sorry-free — multiplicativity is exactly the root property). ","signatureChunk":0}]}